test_mcp_docker	Build and push	2026-10-22T11:15:30.1504497Z             "body": "Hardens the original MCP and independent declarative workflow companion while preserving upstream contracts and defaults. This draft remains incomplete and must not be merged or published as release-ready.\n\nLatest pushed source096b617 adds strict static checking, validated live audit anchors, six-form exact/ambiguous locator fixtures, owned PCM media coverage, production-tarball test exclusion, and lifecycle readiness/full-identity evidence. All57 previously shipped checkout tests are excluded; fresh119-file production-only installed smoke/profile/jobs/journal/guardian checks pass locally. Assertions, timeouts, transport defaults and conservative legacy candidate checks remain intact.\n\nThe new recorded-frame regression deliberately exposes a real unresolved VP9 color-metadata defect: Chromium decodes the owned red frame near[254,0,0], Firefox near[255,24,0], failing the same pixel assertion. Header-only BT.601 control and a temporary one-flag encoder control pass without loosening assertions; restoring the dependency reproduces failure. Dependency is restored byte-for-byte. A reviewable upstream patch is retained, not shipped/published; public recording APIs expose no color option. No hidden artifact rewrite, runtime monkeypatch or system-FFmpeg dependency added.\n\nLocal evidence: Node20/22/24 strict typecheck; graph/cleanup/guardian contracts; locator2/2 and PCM2/2 per LTS; lifecycle artifact8/8 per LTS plus expected-exit1 marker-stall diagnostic; two real deadline cases per LTS retaining original zero-candidate/running assertions. WebKit local execution remains unsupported by host libraries. All193 tracked JS files parse on20/22/24. Dependency audit0 vulnerabilities; limited secret-pattern scan retains the unchanged baseline TLS fixture key.\n\nLatest completed native83 at e95f029:1,937 reported test passes/10 failures, plus Mac actual-client timeout953 and six failed JSON controls. Five176-file production installs, new graph contracts, required typecheck and12 stderr probes pass; native browser deadlines/input/capture/storage, readiness/journal-init failures remain. A new deadline candidate lacks original births/current rows and stays unclassified. One separate full comparison establishes only a narrow same-PID birth mismatch. No historical ownership/debt clearance.\n\nNative84 at096b617 is running, including the known unresolved frame-color test:\n- https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39757905116\n- https://github.com/timmiballz22/playwright-mcp/actions/runs/39757905160\n\nExact commands, hashes, failed controls, native logs and G00–G18 statuses are committed in docs/evidence, docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_LEDGER.md, docs/CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT.md and docs/RELEASE_BLOCKERS.md. No merge/publication or access workaround.\n",
